WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:05.879
Everybody remembered where they were, what
they had been doing, when the SCP Foundation

00:00:05.879 --> 00:00:08.360
revealed themselves to the world.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.809
It was an event that had so fundamentally
changed the lives of every person on Earth

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:17.740
that it became pretty hard to forget that
momentous, horrible day.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.640
Even though, for most people, it had begun
as a day like most others.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.470
Dane Moss had been at home when it started.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.780
His roommates were talking about buying an
air hockey table for their place, something

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.149
to liven up their Saturday nights.

00:00:32.149 --> 00:00:36.120
Even as he half-listened to them discussing
it, Dane figured it would never happen.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:41.340
He was right, of course, but he never could’ve
anticipated the thing that stopped it.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.900
All of them had stopped and fallen silent
as the news report came through.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:50.739
A group calling themselves ‘The SCP Foundation’,
previously responsible for the containment

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:56.649
of anomalous objects, entities, and phenomena,
had declared its new intention to exterminate

00:00:56.649 --> 00:00:58.500
the entire human race.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.219
Dane’s split-second belief that the broadcast
was a Cloverfield-style viral marketing stunt

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:07.939
for a new movie was quickly disproved, when
the ground started to shake.

00:01:07.939 --> 00:01:13.330
Unbeknownst to him, the Foundation was not
only real but had detonated nuclear charges

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:20.990
along the back of SCP-169, an enormous ancient
arthropod that’s body had made up an archipelago

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.650
adrift in the ocean.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:28.470
The detonation caused The Leviathan to stir,
resulting in massive earthquakes and tsunamis.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:32.030
Dane was the only one to make it out of the
apartment alive.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.549
Elsewhere, Joe Rees had been grabbing a coffee
on his way home from work.

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:40.229
He briefly overheard the news report, but
barely paid it any mind.

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:44.909
Then, waiting for his flat white, wondering
what the hold up was, he caught part of a

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:47.689
conversation between two people behind him.

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:49.189
“What is that thing?”

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:50.189
one asked.

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:53.370
“I don’t know, but its face is pure nightmare
fuel,” the other replied.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:57.360
“A bunch of pictures of it just appeared
on everyone’s socials, it’s really freaky

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.990
stuff-”
A sudden shriek went out from a number of

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.759
the coffee shops patrons.

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:07.189
Joe noticed a towering, humanoid shadow being
cast by something behind him; its arms were

00:02:07.189 --> 00:02:12.250
stretched out, disproportionately long…
and it was attacking the two people behind

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.250
him.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:17.900
Acting on an instantaneous fight or flight
response, Joe ran, without looking back to

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.260
see SCP-096 slaughtering everyone that had
seen its face.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.200
Around the same time as the Foundation’s
ominous announcement was played over every

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.819
news channel on the planet, Rene Hudson and
Sky Soto had been on a date.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:37.390
The pair of them had been enjoying hanging
out, playing a few mildly competitive games

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:42.570
at the bowling alley, but there was still
something unspoken lingering in the air.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:47.709
Neither Sky nor Rene really felt any connection;
they liked each other’s company, but that

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:49.510
was as far as it went.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.790
Although neither one of them knew how to broach
the subject for fear of hurting the other’s

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:57.800
feelings, and in the same vein, neither one
of them could have predicted the commotion

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.560
that would happen next.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:04.440
The noise came from outside, the deafening
screams followed by a flood of people running

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.560
for their lives.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:10.390
Hundreds, if not thousands, were fleeing,
any that fell over in the street being trampled

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:16.391
underfoot by everyone behind them, human beings
moving like a mass of ants, clambering over

00:03:16.391 --> 00:03:20.670
each other to get away from a gigantic, ferocious
lizard.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:25.360
Despite the news broadcast declaring themselves
and their intentions to wipe out all humanity,

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.120
nobody on the ground would ever be able to
comprehend just why the Foundation unleashed

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:36.280
SCP-682 and allowed the Hard to Destroy Reptile
to slaughter innocent civilians in droves.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:42.209
While they didn’t know it – or may not
have agreed – Sky, Rene, Dane, and Joe were

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:48.819
all lucky to have survived the initial anomalous
onslaught unleashed by a rogue SCP Foundation.

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:53.410
It did little to ease the pain of being displaced
from their homes, forced to migrate across

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:58.900
the country to join camps of other survivors,
made refugees by anomaly attacks, and the

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.569
efforts of apathetic agents of the Foundation.

00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:06.390
And of the four of them, not one could ever
have predicted the shared fate that awaited

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.390
them.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:12.430
During the months in the wake of the Foundation’s
opening assault on mankind, Rene and Sky had

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:13.659
mostly stuck together.

00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:18.440
They had moved further and further south,
managing to stay safe.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.060
Neither one had thought about their awkward
date in months, they were just grateful to

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.770
have someone they knew to stick together with.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:30.330
Meanwhile, Joe and Dane were hopping from
one refugee camp to the next much the same,

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.060
moving north and eastward respectively.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:37.640
After deploying their first wave of anomalies,
the SCP Foundation’s efforts had shifted

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:42.030
to primarily focus on Groups of Interest that
could pose a threat to their plans.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:46.919
While organizations with knowledge of the
anomalous, like the Global Occult Coalition,

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:51.520
were among the first in their crosshairs,
the civilian population was left living in

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.700
fear, but unscathed.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.280
That is, until the Foundation began targeting
the refugee camps.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:03.150
One of their tactics was to unleash SCP-2241,
a seven-year-old boy with reality warping

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:08.870
powers, into survivor communities to act as
a living weapon, destroying the larger refugee

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:09.870
camps.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:14.220
It was the increased frequency and ruthlessness
of the Foundation’s attacks on human survivors

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:20.340
that forced Sky, Rene, Dane, and Joe to unknowingly
converge on each other.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:25.080
Camps for survivors started getting smaller,
consisting of only a handful of people, in

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:29.650
the hope that this would make it easier for
them to avoid detection by the Foundation.

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:33.630
Arriving and hopping off the back of a jeep
with only the clothes on their backs, the

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:36.500
four strangers exchanged uncertain glances.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:41.410
They had been brought to an abandoned dock,
the wreckage of an overturned cargo ship laying

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.470
on its side in the harbor.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:47.380
Shipping containers were scattered all around,
looking as if they had spilled out of the

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.460
boat onto the dock.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:53.490
The driver of the jeep hadn’t told them
where to go from there, instead, he had just

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.880
driven off without so much as a word.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:06:00.720
The four of them looked around; Dane seemed
particularly unnerved at being so close to

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:05.530
the water, despite it having been months since
the Leviathan settled back to sleep.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:10.030
Suddenly, one of the shipping containers burst
open, and a broad, flannel-shirt wearing man

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.250
stepped out.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:15.860
His face was buried beneath a thick beard,
a shotgun resting against his shoulder as

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.190
he approached the group.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:22.430
The man’s stern, stony expression quickly
changed into a wide grin, as he jovially and

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:25.460
unexpectedly pulled Dane into a hug.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.970
“Welcome, my friends!”

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.720
the man roared with laughter.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:30.720
“Welcome!”

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.650
“Um, who are you?”

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.650
Sky asked.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:37.840
“Of course, allow me to introduce myself,”
he responded, letting go of Dane who needed

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.360
to catch his breath after being squeezed so
much.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:45.660
“My name is Jovanius, for safety I watch
over this camp,” the man announced.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:46.660
“Camp?”

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.130
Joe asked, looking at the wreckage.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:52.420
“The Foundation has been getting more zealous
with targeting those of us that are left,”

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:57.310
Jovanius explained, gesturing for the four
to follow him as he walked back towards the

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.310
container.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.620
“So, we’ve had to take a less conspicuous
approach to surviving.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:06.590
Splitting the camps up into fewer people,
dispersing everyone around a bit more and,

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.590
of course…”

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.610
He swung open the door to the metal container.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:15.759
Inside the cramped space, there were two bunks
either side, one above another, making four

00:07:15.759 --> 00:07:19.350
in total, along with a sleeping bag on the
floor.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:23.130
“Staying in places the Foundation wouldn’t
think to look,” Jovanius continued.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.550
“We have to sleep in here?”

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:26.840
Rene asked in disbelief.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.460
“Better for avoiding detection,” the camp’s
protector replied.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:35.069
“Otherwise, the next camp along is only
twenty minutes away on foot, over in a warehouse;

00:07:35.069 --> 00:07:36.580
if you’d rather go there.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:39.169
But be warned, they have rats.”

00:07:39.169 --> 00:07:43.690
Although it came with a brief adjustment period,
the group quickly acclimatized to living in

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.020
the abandoned dock.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:49.620
Each of them came to appreciate Jovanius’
efforts to keep them all fed with what few

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.250
rations they had.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:57.330
The four of them started calling him Big Joe,
referring to Joe as Lil’ Joe to avoid confusion.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:01.120
Of the group, Dane seemed to have the hardest
time adapting.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:05.990
He was something of a conspiracy theorist,
anxiously talking about other great disasters

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:10.030
throughout human history and wondering if
the Foundation had been responsible for them

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:11.150
all.

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:16.240
Sky felt a little sorry for him, so they decided
to humor his theory that the eruption of Mount

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:22.610
Vesuvius in Pompeii was also the SCP Foundation’s
doing, despite occurring all the way back

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:23.610
in 79 AD.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:29.330
Through all their various concerns about surviving
in this anomalous, apocalyptic world, Big

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:32.810
Jo seemed to have a talent for keeping the
group’s spirits up.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:37.360
Whether it was by recounting them all with
folk stories or turning bland food rations

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:42.500
into more flavorful meals, he made the four
of them feel safe, especially with his weapon

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:43.930
never far away.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:46.410
That is, until one evening.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:52.290
A glowing red streak shot through the air
not far from camp, catching Jovanius’ immediate

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.290
attention.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:57.910
It was an emergency flare, sent up by the
neighboring camp at the warehouse.

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.279
Something was wrong.

00:08:59.279 --> 00:09:05.149
Grabbing his shotgun and urging Sky, Dane,
Rene, and Lil’ Joe to stay put, Big Jo left,

00:09:05.149 --> 00:09:08.570
running off into the growing dark of night
to try and help.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:12.890
The whole group stayed awake waiting for their
protector to return, the next hour feeling

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:13.890
like an eternity.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:18.250
By the time he returned, the sun had fully
set outside.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:22.610
Even by the low light of their lamps inside
the container, it was clear by his face that

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:25.829
any and all optimism had drained out of Jovanius.

00:09:25.829 --> 00:09:34.050
“There was nothing left, all of them were…
gone,” he explained, unable to believe what

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:35.050
he had seen.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.820
“There was this… oil everywhere.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:41.589
Corrosive, like an acid, just burning through
what was left of them.”

00:09:41.589 --> 00:09:46.240
Trying to regain some semblance of composure,
he urged the group to get some sleep, reassuring

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.769
them that they would be safe for the rest
of the night.

00:09:48.769 --> 00:09:53.079
Not one of them realized just how wrong they
were… or that they’d never seen Jovanius

00:09:53.079 --> 00:09:55.430
again after they fell asleep.

00:09:55.430 --> 00:10:00.140
Rene was the first to discover he had gone
missing, screaming with panic, waking up Sky

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:01.579
and the two boys.

00:10:01.579 --> 00:10:04.980
After they had calmed her down, Sky tried
to rationalize what was going on.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:09.310
They were as worried about Big Jo as the others,
but couldn’t afford to lose their nerve

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:12.769
and potentially attract the attention of a
Foundation kill squad.

00:10:12.769 --> 00:10:15.339
“It’s the Foundation,” Dane babbled,
terrified.

00:10:15.339 --> 00:10:16.570
“They’ve found us.

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:18.630
They’re closing in, oh man!”

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:19.860
“Relax,” Sky replied.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.190
“All of you chill.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:24.830
There are other camps nearby, maybe Big Jo
went to check on them too?

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:28.060
See if what had happened to the warehouse
group happened anywhere else?”

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.000
“You don’t think he would have told us?”

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.360
Lil’ Joe retorted, seeming to be the least
concerned about Jovanius’ whereabouts.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.690
“We were asleep.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:37.279
It’s not like him to wake us.

00:10:37.279 --> 00:10:39.370
He knows we’d worry,” Sky answered.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:41.329
“What if he’s dead?”

00:10:41.329 --> 00:10:42.329
Rene sobbed.

00:10:42.329 --> 00:10:43.870
“Don’t say that!”

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:44.870
they replied.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:45.870
“She’s right though.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:49.100
He left his shotgun right here,” Joe interjected
again.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.540
“Whatever got the warehouse group killed
him, it's obvious.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:55.350
At least I don’t have to go by that stupid
nickname anymore.”

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:56.950
“What the hell, man?”

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:57.950
Dane yelled.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.220
“You joking at a time like this?

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:00.500
What’s wrong with you?”

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.329
There was an uncomfortably long pause.

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:07.320
Everyone in the container turned to look at
Joe, leaning against one of the metal walls

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.320
with his arms folded.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:12.640
The other three were all thinking the same
thing, although Dane was the first to say

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:13.640
it aloud.

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.440
“You killed him, didn’t you?”

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.040
“Don’t be ridiculous!”

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:20.899
Joe chastised him, backing away slightly,
betraying his own little hint of fear.

00:11:20.899 --> 00:11:23.700
“You and Rene are hysterical; you both need
to calm down and-”

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.340
Before Joe could finish his sentence, a withered
arm reached out of the wall and grabbed his

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:29.340
throat.

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:33.750
It looked like the rotting, decaying arm of
a corpse, protruding out of a puddle of black

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:38.279
mucus that now seemed to be spreading across
the inner wall of the container.

00:11:38.279 --> 00:11:42.900
Rene screamed in horror as more of the black
substance oozed from the arm, melting away

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:45.490
Joe as it held him helplessly in its grip.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:51.070
It was then that a face peered through the
oily patch smeared on the wall: the nightmarish

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:55.200
visage of SCP-106, the Old Man.

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:59.640
For a second, Sky thought about trying to
help Joe, they could’ve pulled him free,

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:01.339
but it was already too late.

00:12:01.339 --> 00:12:05.760
The corrosion was spreading, it looked like
it would melt them too if they so much as

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:06.850
touched it…

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.089
Joe was gone.

00:12:08.089 --> 00:12:12.060
The remaining three of them burst out of the
shipping container they had called home, afraid

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.100
for their lives.

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.830
“What the hell was that?”

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:15.830
Dane screamed.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:16.880
“Oh man, I knew it.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.730
They’ve sent a monster after us.”

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:23.540
Sky barely paid him any mind, their attention
grabbed by movement nearby.

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:27.190
Someone had started running the second they
had exited the shipping crate; they had been

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:28.779
watching from a distance.

00:12:28.779 --> 00:12:30.139
“Hey, stop!”

00:12:30.139 --> 00:12:32.800
Sky yelled, about to run after them when…

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:33.800
“Sky…”

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.470
Rene’s voice was cracking under the weight
of her terror.

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:37.470
Turning around, they saw it.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:39.660
The Old Man stood behind Rene.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:44.290
It looked even more grotesque under the low
light provided by several distant fires in

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:49.960
the ruins of cities the Foundation had destroyed,
giving the horizon a hellish glow.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:57.230
SCP-106’s withered, lipless face bore his
rotting teeth, locked in a skull-like grin;

00:12:57.230 --> 00:13:01.800
it gave a sense he was gaining some twisted
enjoyment out of what he did next.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:08.200
Rene had been frozen to the spot, sniffling
in fear, her legs rigid and locked in place.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:12.570
Until the Old Man clamped a hand over her
shoulder, then she cried out in a blood-curdling

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:14.320
shriek of agony.

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:19.399
More of the black ooze spilled from his emaciated
fingers, dripping down her front while Sky

00:13:19.399 --> 00:13:21.240
looked on in terror.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:25.560
Rene had been the one person who had been
with them the entire time, from the moment

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:28.050
the Foundation unleashed hell.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:31.890
Every camp they moved to Rene was in the same
one with them.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:35.769
The pair of them may not have been a couple,
but she had been the only constant in this

00:13:35.769 --> 00:13:37.649
anomalous apocalypse.

00:13:37.649 --> 00:13:42.019
And now, this sinister SCP was killing her.

00:13:42.019 --> 00:13:46.050
Fighting their every urge to grab Rene and
pull her free, Sky instead let themselves

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.390
be led away by Dane.

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:51.899
Choking back tears, they ran alongside him
in the direction of whoever had been watching

00:13:51.899 --> 00:13:52.899
them.

00:13:52.899 --> 00:13:56.699
The shadowy figure was just about visible,
although definitely still close enough to

00:13:56.699 --> 00:13:57.720
be heard.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:02.649
In the dark, there was the sound of a fall,
accompanied by a pained grunt indicating that

00:14:02.649 --> 00:14:05.430
whoever had been watching the container had
tripped.

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:08.000
Both Dane and Sky knew this was their chance.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:12.590
Together, they lunged at the figure before
he had a chance to scramble back to his feet,

00:14:12.590 --> 00:14:15.699
with Dane pinning the observer down by his
wrists.

00:14:15.699 --> 00:14:20.019
That was when the light of the burning city
on the horizon illuminated his face: he was

00:14:20.019 --> 00:14:25.240
the jeep driver, the one who had dropped them
at Jovanius’ camp to begin with, the only

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:30.279
other person – apart from Big Jo – who
knew where their camp was.

00:14:30.279 --> 00:14:31.279
“You!”

00:14:31.279 --> 00:14:32.279
Sky declared.

00:14:32.279 --> 00:14:33.500
“What were you doing spying on us?”

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:36.670
“I have nothing to say to you,” the man
spat.

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:38.149
“Answer their question!”

00:14:38.149 --> 00:14:41.620
Dane yelled, slapping the man in the face,
although he didn’t seem to react.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.300
“What is that thing chasing us?

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:44.579
Why did it kill our friends?”

00:14:44.579 --> 00:14:47.610
“You might as well tell us,” Sky told
him calmly.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.300
“After all, once that monster catches up,
we’ll all be dead.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:53.089
You were watching expecting a result, right?

00:14:53.089 --> 00:14:57.170
Had to make sure none of us made it; not that
there’s anyone left for us to tell if we

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.260
did survive.”

00:14:58.260 --> 00:14:59.459
“He’s with the Foundation!”

00:14:59.459 --> 00:15:01.430
Dane gasped, catching on quickly.

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:05.470
“You had them send that corpse-thing to
kill us, man?”

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:08.459
“SCP-106,” the undercover MTF agent corrected.

00:15:08.459 --> 00:15:11.180
“And yeah, it’s here because we sent it.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:13.279
You all went underground, hiding in your little
camps.

00:15:13.279 --> 00:15:15.490
We had to look even closer to find you all.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:18.430
Ungrateful, all of you.”

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:19.750
“Ungrateful?”

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:23.889
Sky exploded, enraged and offended at the
idea anyone could justify all the death the

00:15:23.889 --> 00:15:25.930
Foundation had unleashed on the world.

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:30.370
“What, you expect us to thank you for hunting
your fellow human beings to extinction?

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.079
Dropping nightmare after nightmare on us?

00:15:32.079 --> 00:15:34.009
And we’re meant to be grateful for that?”

00:15:34.009 --> 00:15:38.279
“None of you understand what we’re trying
to do,” the Foundation agent replied without

00:15:38.279 --> 00:15:39.330
a hint of remorse.

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:44.360
“What we’re trying to do is bigger, more
important than your mundane little lives.

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:50.050
The only way we can save humanity – from
It – is by wiping you out.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:55.540
Before either Sky or Dane could ask what ‘It’
was, a gloopy, oily smear appeared on the

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:56.540
ground.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:16:00.680
Clawing his way out of it, the Old Man reached
for the MTF operative, disintegrating him

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.500
like it had done before.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.779
But the agent barely reacted, didn’t cry
out like Rene or Joe had.

00:16:06.779 --> 00:16:13.290
He was still, even as he was melted by the
slimy black secretion of SCP-106; it was as

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:17.829
if the man couldn’t feel the pain of what
was happening to him as he died.

00:16:17.829 --> 00:16:21.550
A splatter of the same corrosive mucus spread
onto Dane’s sleeve.

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:25.709
Freaking out as it began burning through his
jacket, he desperately tried to wipe it off,

00:16:25.709 --> 00:16:29.870
only to smear it, spreading the dissolving
substance further and crying out as he felt

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:34.290
it eating into the palms of his hands.

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:38.540
SCP-106 climbed up out of its oily puddle,
dropping the disintegrating MTF agent.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:44.220
He disappeared into the corrosive pool, vanishing
from sight like he’d fallen into a ditch.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:48.970
Sky backed away, their eyes locked with the
sunken stare of the Old Man, feeling their

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:52.820
legs begin to freeze in fear, just like Rene’s.

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:53.820
“G-gun…”

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:59.190
Dane rasped, laying at SCP-106’s feet, slowly
succumbing to the same fate that had befallen

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:00.190
the others.

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:03.510
“Big Jo’s… gun…” he rasped again.

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:07.660
With the last of his strength, he used his
arm to grab the Old Man’s ankle, howling

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:12.010
in pain as more of the black substance oozed
from the monster’s wrinkled flesh.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:16.740
Sky turn and raced back towards the shipping
container, hardly daring to look over their

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:17.829
shoulder.

00:17:17.829 --> 00:17:22.329
Every movement, every tiny shift of shadow
they detected in the corner of their eye,

00:17:22.329 --> 00:17:27.299
filled their mind with images of the Old Man
baring down on them, wearing that sadistic,

00:17:27.299 --> 00:17:28.740
skeletal grin.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:33.680
Sky pulled the heavy metal door open, using
all their strength to get back inside.

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:37.910
Their arms were numbed, trembling so much
with terror that it was like they weren’t

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.360
attached properly.

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:43.810
They fumbled about in the dark, their fingers
brushing up against the weapon, resting in

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:46.170
the corner where Jovanius had left it.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:50.830
Pulling on the pump, Sky turned, the gun raised,
knowing that the Old Man was right behind

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:52.940
them, and pulled the trigger…

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:59.410
It gave a redundant click; it was empty, no
ammunition – the gun had been just for show.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:03.940
SCP-106 reached for the weapon and pulled
it from Sky’s hands, the metal of it slowly

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:08.140
melting as it was coated in the tar-like corrosive
substance.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:12.559
Recoiling their hands from it, Sky went to
dash for the door, only to feel the Old Man’s

00:18:12.559 --> 00:18:17.630
bony, burning fingers hook into their back
and drag them towards the greasy black stain

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:21.440
he was leaning out of, pulling them into his
domain.

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:26.679
The world had been a living nightmare since
the Foundation had revealed itself, and unleashed

00:18:26.679 --> 00:18:30.210
an anomalous apocalypse on humanity.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:35.650
But SCP-106’s pocket dimension might just
have been worse…

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:41.380
Now go and check out “SCP-5000 THE FULL
STORY COMPILATION” and “SCP-106 CONTAINMENT

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:46.580
BREACH” if you’d like a little more of
this particular flavor of existential nightmare!

